mlx-dfloat is an independent reader and decoder for the DFloat11 checkpoint format. It is not a fork of DFloat11
and is not affiliated with the DFloat11 authors.

DFloat11
--------
The DFloat11 method and checkpoint format come from:

  Tianyi Zhang, Mohsen Hariri, Shaochen Zhong, Vipin Chaudhary, Yang Sui, Xia Hu, Anshumali Shrivastava.
  "70% Size, 100% Accuracy: Lossless LLM Compression for Efficient GPU Inference via Dynamic-Length Float
  (DFloat11)". arXiv:2504.11651, https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.11651. The paper is distributed under the
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (CC BY 4.0).

The authors' implementation is https://github.com/LeanModels/DFloat11, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. The format reader and the decoders in this package are a separate implementation of the published
format. The only file taken from that repository is the test-only encoder described below.

Test-only encoder and test data
-------------------------------
tests/_upstream/dfloat11_encoder.py is derived from dfloat11_utils.py of https://github.com/LeanModels/DFloat11 at
commit 457733886c, Copyright 2025 Tianyi Zhang, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. It builds test fixtures,
and one group it built ships in the package (long_codes.npz); the encoder code itself is not installed.
tests/_upstream/NOTICE lists the changes made to it.

src/mlx_dfloat/_canary_data/ holds a small slice (four compressed blocks of one matrix) of the DFloat11/Qwen3-4B-DF11
checkpoint and the matching BF16 values from Qwen/Qwen3-4B, which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The
slice and long_codes.npz (the group built by the encoder above) are installed with the package as check data for the GPU
decoder.

mflux
-----
The optional FLUX.1 integration (the mlx-dfloat[mflux] extra) and the benchmark run on mflux,
https://github.com/mflux-community/mflux, Copyright (c) 2026 Filip Strand, licensed under the MIT License. mflux is a
dependency installed separately; mlx-dfloat does not include its code.

Model weights
-------------
mlx-dfloat ships no model weights. A DFloat11 checkpoint carries the licence of the model it was compressed from;
FLUX.1-dev and FLUX.1-Krea-dev, for example, are under Black Forest Labs' non-commercial licence.
